{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Moses said, etc., and you shall give them.</b> He said ״וּנְתַתֶּם לָהֶם״ — which makes it appear as though they are the ones giving — yet immediately afterward Scripture says ״וַיִּתֵּן לָהֶם מֹשֶׁה וְגוֹ׳ אֶת מַמְלֶכֶת״ and so forth (Numbers 32:33). This is because the giving is not finalized until after the condition is fulfilled; therefore he said <b>and you shall give.</b> But it remains to be understood why he said <b>וּנְתַתֶּם</b> — he should have said ״תִּתְּנוּ לָהֶם״. Perhaps he alluded to them the very things he said to the children of Gad and the children of Reuben: that if they go — all Israel will succeed, both those who take their inheritance in the land and those who take their inheritance across the Jordan. And this is what he means by <b>if they cross</b> etc. <b>and we shall conquer</b> etc. — the success of those who inherit the land; <b>and you shall give</b> etc. — the success of those who inherit across the Jordan. And this allusion would not have been heard if he had said ״תִּתְּנוּ לָהֶם״."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:57.485717451Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}